# The shared terminology of Termablo's translations: every name and game
# concept that must read the same everywhere, and each language's style.
# The translation and review prompts carry all of it; `i18n check` warns
# where a translated line drops a term its English uses.
#
# A term lists, per language, the forms that count as using it, the
# dictionary form first; list inflected forms too where the language
# declines (Russian: "Уголь", "Угля"...). "-" keeps the English word.
# The world bible is docs/lore.md (docs/lore.ru.md in Russian).
{
  style: {
    all: """
- Tone: spare, grave, a little weary. Dark fantasy in the line of Diablo. Short sentences. No modern idioms, no jokes the English does not make, no extra exclamation marks.
- The player is addressed directly, as one person ("you").
- Proper names (people, places, bosses, unique items) are capitalized as names in your language.
- Numbers stay as digits. Keyboard keys (g, tab, esc, ctrl+c, hjkl, Q) stay as they are.
- Item names: bases are nouns with a gender; magic prefixes, rare first words and articles agree with them through gender forms.
- Two lights: Ember-light is warm (torches, braziers, the forge, fire) and came from below; cold light is the Oracle's (marsh lights, crystals, wisps). Keep "warm" and "cold" in the words for them.
"""
    de: """
- Address the player with "du" (informal), as German RPGs do. Capitalize "du" only at the start of a sentence.
- Use German quotation marks „…“ for speech.
- Item bases as German compound nouns where natural (Kettenhemd, Kriegshammer). Genders: m, f, n, pl.
- Articles agree: write ref.the and ref.a with gender forms (der/die/das, ein/eine/ein).
"""
    fr: """
- Address the player with "vous".
- Use French guillemets « … » for speech, with a space inside them, and a space before ! ? : ;.
- Adjectives usually follow the noun: write item.magic as "{base} {prefix} {suffix}" and agree prefixes with the base: genders m, f, mp, fp; mv and fv for nouns that elide the article (l'arme).
- Articles agree: write ref.the as { m: "le {name}", f: "la {name}", mv: "l'{name}", fv: "l'{name}", mp: "les {name}", fp: "les {name}" }.
"""
    it: """
- Address the player with "tu" (informal).
- Use Italian guillemets «…» for speech.
- Adjectives usually follow the noun: write item.magic as "{base} {prefix} {suffix}" and agree prefixes with the base: genders m, f, mp, fp; mv and fv for nouns that elide the article (l'arma).
- Articles agree: il/lo/la/l'/i/gli/le. Pick lo for masculine nouns starting with s+consonant or z by giving them gender m with a lo- article in their own variant if needed, or phrase around it.
"""
    ru: """
- Address the player with "вы" (lowercase).
- Use «ёлочки» for speech, „лапки“ inside them. Write ё.
- Russian has no articles: write ref.the and ref.a as "{name}". Monster names are nouns with gender m, f, n or pl.
- Item names: prefixes agree with the base in gender (Зазубренный кинжал, Зазубренная булава, Зазубренные сапоги). Suffixes "of the Wolf" become genitive phrases (волка) or adjectives, whichever reads like a Diablo item.
- The Russian lore (docs/lore.ru.md) set the names; follow it.
"""
    ar: """
- Modern Standard Arabic. Address the player in the masculine singular, as Arabic games do.
- No diacritics (harakat): the terminal drops them. Use Western digits (0-9).
- Use «…» for speech.
- The game lays the text out right to left; write it in logical order as usual. Keep Latin text out of sentences except keyboard keys.
- Adjectives follow the noun and agree in gender (m, f). Non-human plurals agree as feminine singular. Write item.magic as "{base} {prefix} {suffix}".
- Arabic has a definite article but no indefinite one: ref.the is "{name}" when names carry ال already, ref.a is "{name}".
"""
    zh: """
- Simplified Chinese. Use full-width punctuation (，。！？：；“”) and no spaces between Chinese words; numbers stay half-width digits.
- A Chinese character takes two terminal cells: keep the short UI labels short (# max counts cells).
- No articles, no gender: ref.the and ref.a are "{name}"; nouns are plain strings.
- Item names read like Chinese ARPG loot: write item.magic in the order that reads naturally, for example "{suffix}{prefix}{base}" with suffixes like "之狼" or "狼之".
- Follow the conventions of Chinese Diablo localizations: 精英 for champion, 暗金 for unique items, 稀有 rare, 魔法 magic.
"""
  }

